zabbix-widget-event-timeline (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * RPM only: relaxed the PHP dependency from "php >= 8.1" to
    "(php >= 8.1 or php-common >= 8.1)" so that the package stays
    installable when the php metapackage is absent (e.g. while switching
    from PHP 8.3 to php8.4-* packages). Minimum PHP version unchanged.
    No changes to the DEB dependencies or the widget code.

 -- claude <noreply@example.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

zabbix-widget-event-timeline (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added the Trigger Selection receiving foundation (v0.2.0 Phase 1): in
    addition to fixed triggers, the widget now accepts a _triggerids
    broadcast (plain triggerids[]) from e.g. Metric Navigator 0.4.2+.
    Resolved independently of the Host Selection (TriggerSelection::resolve()).
    In Phase 1 the received state is only exposed for inspection; event
    extraction and aggregation results are identical to 0.1.5.
  * Renamed the configuration field label from "Events" to "Triggers".
  * Added includes/TriggerSelection.php to the RPM/DEB file lists.

 -- claude <noreply@example.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

zabbix-widget-event-timeline (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Switched the release workflow to a compact release-branch model
    (release/vX.Y.Z -> PR to main, merged after review/testing, tags and
    Releases created on main going forward). No functional or packaging
    content changes beyond the version bump from 0.1.4.
  * Carried forward the README/spec description updates that brought the
    documented behaviour in line with the 0.1.4 implementation (configurable
    week-start day, ui/modules-first install path, etc.).

